From c27fdb59903f343dff5255ca51560f4faeebb467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:15:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] feat(xcloud): latency-based region, automatic quality
 and real stream statistics

- Region: "Lowest measured latency" times a TCP connection to the gateway
  of each region Microsoft's login offers this account (five samples,
  DNS excluded) and only leaves Microsoft's default for a region that
  answers at least 15 ms and 15 % faster; kept 20 minutes. Nothing is
  added to the region list and the sign-in is untouched.
- Statistics: both players read WebRTC's own getStats() every 2 s
  (resolution, fps, codec, round trip, jitter, packet loss, bitrate,
  decode time, dropped frames, region, state). The web player gets them
  from the peer connection player.js creates, through a document-start
  script; player.js is unchanged. The last stream and a short history
  are saved and shown in a new Statistics section of the Xbox Cloud
  settings, with the measured latency per region and the phone's H.264
  decoder. Values WebRTC does not report show as unknown.
- Automatic quality (on unless a bitrate limit is set): after a stream
  that lost over 2 % of its packets the next is capped at 80 % of the
  rate it reached; clean streams raise the cap again.
- Performance and Xbox Cloud profiles pick the lowest-latency region.

Diagnostics and downloads:
- The shared logs get timings.txt (also for a start that never reached
  the screen), memory.txt (memory and thermal state) and the x86-64
  launcher's log with its renderer choice.
- A start that takes over 90 s offers "Share logs" on the loading
  screen while it still runs.
- The ARMv8.0 Proton download shows its real size on disk on the loading
  screen; an interrupted download resumes (tested against a local
  server with ranges).
- The Performance profile is called "Maximum safe performance".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
